SUMMARY:Historical Overview
DESCRIPTION:University Establishment Al-Qadisiyah University was established in 1987 as one of Iraq&rsquo;s public universities. The university started with a limited number of colleges and scientific departments, then gradually expanded to include 18 colleges covering various scientific and humanities disciplines.\nDevelopment Phases Phase One (1987-1995) Establishment of core colleges (Education, Arts, Science) Building the initial university infrastructure Recruiting distinguished teaching staff Phase Two (1995-2005) Opening Medicine, Engineering, and Law colleges Developing laboratories and libraries Expanding graduate programs Phase Three (2005-2015) Establishing new colleges (Pharmacy, Dentistry, Nursing) Updating curricula according to international standards Enhancing international cooperation with global universities Current Phase (2015-Present) Developing digital infrastructure Adopting blended e-learning Pursuing international academic accreditations Achievements Graduating more than 100,000 students since establishment Publishing thousands of research papers in peer-reviewed journals Achieving advanced positions in international rankings 
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
